  "body": "## What happens\n\nWhole-model contour bands (#2460) use the same `emit_band` function as the tabbed levels. Each band places its tab windows on its own ring.\n\nIf a band boundary lies inside the tab height, the windows of the two bands may not line up. The reviewer says the tab is then shorter than `tab_height`. The part stays held by the lowest band.\n\nSource: second review of PR #2486 at head `b755c8e4b`, non-blocker N1. The reviewer says the point came from #2460, not from PR #2486, and that a P7 follow-up is enough.\n\nThe review uses \"may\". It does not confirm wrong output. This issue has no `bug` label for that reason.\n\n## What is wanted\n\n- A test with a band boundary inside the tab height. It checks the windows of both bands.\n- Either the windows line up across the boundary, or the short tab gets a `tabs:` note.\n\n## Not addressed\n\nPR #2486 does not address this point. The PR comments do not show a fix for it.\n\n## Done means\n\n- The test is in `crates/motion/tests/`.\n- The output either lines up across the boundary, or it gives a note.\n\nFound in the review of PR #2486. Origin: #2460.\n",
